  "name": "Fetch a surveil land at their end step, lands stay on top",
  "intent": "At the opponent's end step with fewer than four lands out, crack a fetch for a surveil land, Hedge Maze first, then Thundering Falls, then Commercial District, and surveil only a creature with mana value 4 or more into the graveyard so Living End returns it; a smaller creature (Shardless Agent, Endurance, mana value 3, wanted for its own triggered/evoke value rather than as Living End fodder) stays on top instead, the same threshold open-land-idle's own surveil answer uses. A land, a fetchland included, stays on top either way: the cascade turn still needs it. From four lands fetch-surveil-land bins lands instead. Only at 6 life or more and while fewer than two surveil lands are out.",
